{%- comment -%}
  collection.fye-options — fragment template, NOT a customer-facing page.

  Added 04/09/2026. Feeds the ring matchmaker's option photographs: each option
  tile shows a real ring matching everything chosen so far, so picking Halo
  makes every cut tile a halo, and picking sapphire makes them all sapphires
  (Ed, 04/09/2026 — "wherever possible, subsequent choices reflect previous
  choices").

  Hand-picking could not reach this: 7 styles x 10 cuts is 70 photographs
  before shoulders are considered. This is one request per step instead.

    /collections/engagement-rings?filter.p.m.filters.ring_style=Halo&view=fye-options

  Returns compact JSON — one entry per product, its image and its filter
  values — and assets/fye-ui.js picks the first product matching each option.

  WHY ALL THE KEYS AT ONCE. Liquid cannot read a query parameter, so this
  template cannot be told which metafield the current step is asking about.
  It therefore emits every key the finder uses, and the JavaScript selects.
  Twelve short values per product; 50 products is around 10KB, a couple
  gzipped.

  50 IS A DELIBERATE CEILING. It covers the common values comfortably. A rare
  option whose only stock sits past the fiftieth product simply gets no
  photograph, which is survivable — and honest, since it is genuinely rare.

  Do not link to this. With no layout it renders as bare JSON.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- layout none -%}
{%- liquid
  assign keys = 'ring_style,shoulder_style,stone_type,stone_shape,centre_weight,profile,band_width,weight,metal_colour,carat,setting,eternity_style' | split: ','
-%}
{
  "count": {{ collection.products_count | default: 0 }},
  "products": [
    {%- assign rows = 0 -%}
    {%- for product in collection.products limit: 50 -%}
      {%- if product.featured_image == nil -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- if rows > 0 -%},{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign rows = rows | plus: 1 -%}
      {
        "img": {{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 240 | json }},
        "url": {{ product.url | json }},
        "v": {
          {%- assign wrote = 0 -%}
          {%- for key in keys -%}
            {%- assign mf = product.metafields.filters[key] -%}
            {%- if mf == nil or mf.value == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
            {%- if wrote > 0 -%},{%- endif -%}
            {%- assign wrote = wrote | plus: 1 -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              A list-type metafield arrives as an array. Joining on a pipe keeps
              the payload flat; fye-ui.js splits on it and tests membership, so a
              ring tagged with several settings matches any of them.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- if mf.type contains 'list.' -%}
              {{ key | json }}: {{ mf.value | join: '|' | json }}
            {%- else -%}
              {{ key | json }}: {{ mf.value | json }}
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        }
      }
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
